 the core members of the crime-fighting  team as a mutant with the ability to  influence electronics through his own  bio electric field bedlam definitely  played a pivotal role in several  missions and like he says in the movie  he really can directly affect people's  brains which came in handy when the  citizens of San Francisco were turned  into brainwashed  bees and bedlam was able to reverse the  brainwashing without destroying them all  but once upon the time bedlam almost  destroyed the planet in x-force number  87 bedlam left the x-force to join up  with his long-lost brother Christopher  on a team called the new hellions bedlam  later finds out that in a series of jerk  moves Christopher had killed their  parents 14 years earlier and was now  planning to revive a mutant named  Armageddon man with the power to sweep  the world with natural disasters in  other words it was a bad family reunion  realizing the error of his ways  bedlam rejoins x-force to put a stop to  Armageddon man and they all learn a  valuable lesson about friendship  Vanisher you don't see a lot of banasur  in deadpool 2 which makes Brad Pitt's  eventual cameo all the more shocking the  Vanisher of the comics is much different  than the one we see or rather don't see  in the movie first gracing the pages of  uncanny x-men number two the Vanisher  was one of the OG x-men foes a  teleporting mutants who like to rob  banks and steal government secrets  decades later Vanisher was still living  a life of crime when x-force tracked him  down gave him a brain tumor and forced  him to teleport them around to their  battles essentially turning him into  their indentured slave in a long career  filled with dark moments this was  definitely one of the x-force's darkest  and it proved that they were willing to  go to any lengths to get a job done now  under deadpool likes them so much black  Tom Cassidy black Tom Cassidy's biggest  contribution in Deadpool 2 is giving  Deadpool an excuse to grief Gaye below  for who he chooses to shoot but in the  comics he has a much bigger role black  Tom is a mutant infected with the same  techno-organic virus that affects cable  just like in the movie black Tom was  incarcerated at the same prison as  juggernaut and he was also shot by cable  here's where the two paths diverged  however in the comics after cable shoots  him black Tom gets healed and gains the  ability to control plants because why  not and also gains Deadpool's healing  factor  exactly the kind of villain that could  come back to haunt Deadpool especially  if another Deadpool movie takes up the  recent adventures theme of everything we  do has consequences  but maybe without the plan thing that  might be too weird even by Deadpool  standards Russell  since Deadpool - basically served as the  origin story for Russell Collins aka  fire fist it made sure to hit some of  the characters notes from the comics  fire fists origin story saw him as a  Navy recruit who suddenly discovers his  fiery powers gets locked up and breaks  free x-factor shows up to fight him then  lets him join the team and then in the  events leading up to x-force number 24  Russell is imprisoned by a mutant hating  group called the Friends of humanity  leaving the x-force to mount a rescue  operation while he's in transit pretty  much what happened in Deadpool - but  with fewer crotches landing on cables  face but his biggest contributions to  x-force have been well giving them  something to fight not once but twice  has he been brainwashed and turned to  the dark side in the comics once for  every finger he can give we're not sure  where his character will go in any  upcoming films but one thing's for sure  they sure picked a hell of a kid to  rescue Domino when you break it right  down Domino has some of the most useful  powers in the whole film and she's used  them plenty of times in the comics to  get both Deadpool and cable out of tight  spots she also gets one of the coolest  sequences in the movie when she wants to  she could even get the best of Deadpool  with just a few well-timed words which  makes her one of the most formidable  mutants on the team any future Deadpool  film is bound to feature a ton of Domino  showing off how powerful she really is  and despite what Deadpool may say about  it that's a pretty useful ability yes it  is let's meet in the middle and say no  it isn't Hope Summers leave it to  Deadpool to introduce one of the most  powerful mutants in the world and then  end her brief story so tragically we're  talking about hope summers of course  cable's daughter and the whole reason he  traveled back in time in the first place  in the comics hope is what's known as an  omega-level mutant basically just  unstoppably powerful after Cyclops  becomes Dark Phoenix and Avengers vs.  x-men number 11 hope harnesses the  Phoenix force to become an  even more powerful Phoenix and stop it  and an uncanny x-men number 541 hope  absorbs all of the x-men's powers to put  a stop to an out-of-control juggernaut  where does it end well in x-men legacy  number 263 she admits that she's never  seen the true limits of her powers  now that cabl has successfully stopped  her death hope summers could have a big  role to play in whatever on-screen form  the x-force takes next Yukio and Shatter  star in the film shatter star is a  sword-wielding mutants from mojo world  in the comics he's also a sword-wielding  mutant for mojo world along with some  extra weirdness that made him his own  dad's father but that's not where we're  going here after a long history in the  comics x-factor number 45 had shatter  star come out as gay and featured a  panel of him and fellow male mutants  Richter locking lips the Internet was  quick to praise the writers of Deadpool  - for featuring a gay superhero but now  that the movie is out and the only thing  shadows are shattered were some  helicopter blades all the attention in  that arena falls on Yukio who is now in  an on-screen relationship with negasonic  teenage warhead while Marvel movies have  technically featured LGBTQ characters  before Deadpool - puts that  representation right in the forefront  but only after making everyone think  that it was going to come from somewhere  else that's pure Deadpool thanks for  watching click the looper icon to  subscribe to our YouTube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  you love to  [Music]

